---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import ExploreNext from "../../../components/ExploreNext.astro";
---

<Layout title="Restoring a 1970 Puch Maxi">
  <article class="puchProject">
    <header class="hero reveal">
      <a href="/projects#build" class="backLink">← Projects</a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Build and Research</p>
      <h1 class="title">Restoring a 1970 Puch Maxi.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        I bought it in Cambridge knowing nothing about engines. Before it became dependable enough
        to ride to London, I broke most things on it at least once.
      </p>
    </header>

    <figure class="heroImage reveal">
      <img
        src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/road-to-london.webp"
        alt="View from the Puch Maxi while riding at 30 miles per hour"
        width="1800"
        height="1350"
        loading="eager"
        decoding="async"
      />
      <figcaption>Eventually: Cambridge to London, at about thirty miles per hour.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="section reveal opening">
      <p class="eyebrow">The premise</p>
      <h2 class="sectionTitle">It had to get worse before it got better.</h2>
      <p>
        The Puch arrived with buckets of character and a loose interpretation of reliability:
        no throttle grips, no tail light and a succession of fuel, brake and engine problems.
        Working through them taught me the basic systems of a combustion engine—not in a tidy
        sequence, but by making blunders, finding the consequences and trying again.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="arrivalGrid reveal" aria-label="The Puch Maxi on arrival">
      <figure class="listing">
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/ebay-listing.webp" alt="The original eBay listing for the Puch Maxi" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>The listing.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure class="arrival">
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/newly-arrived.webp" alt="The Puch Maxi shortly after arriving" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>Newly arrived in Cambridge.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/no-throttle-grips.webp" alt="The Puch Maxi handlebars without throttle grips" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>No grips on the throttle.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/no-tail-light.webp" alt="The rear of the Puch Maxi without a tail light" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>No tail light either.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Fuel and fire</p>
      <h2 class="sectionTitle">Learning by following the fault.</h2>
      <p>
        A leaking petcock and fuel line led into carburation and combustion. The first successful
        starts were not graceful—the engine coughed, smoked and cleared its throat—but they were
        the first proof that the collection of parts could become a vehicle again.
      </p>
      <div class="fuelPair">
        <figure>
          <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/leaky-petcock.webp" alt="Fuel leaking from the Puch Maxi petcock" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          <figcaption>Tracing a fuel leak to the petcock.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure class="videoFigure">
          <video controls playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/docs/puch-maxi/images/newly-arrived.webp">
            <source src="/docs/puch-maxi/video/clearing-its-throat.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
          </video>
          <figcaption>The engine clearing its throat on an early start.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section reveal">
      <p class="eyebrow">Brakes</p>
      <h2 class="sectionTitle">Taking the wheel off—and putting it back.</h2>
      <p>
        The broken back brake required a wheel removal, a new brake and the more consequential
        challenge of reassembling everything correctly. It was typical of the restoration: a
        modest fault opening into several unfamiliar jobs.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="brakeSequence reveal" aria-label="Replacing the rear brake">
      <figure>
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/broken-back-brake.webp" alt="The broken rear brake on the Puch Maxi" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>01 · The broken back brake.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/wheel-off.webp" alt="The Puch Maxi with its rear wheel removed" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>02 · Wheel off.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/changing-back-brake.webp" alt="Replacing the Puch Maxi rear brake" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>03 · Changing the brake.</figcaption>
      </figure>
      <figure>
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/brake-change-smiley.webp" alt="A smiley face drawn during the brake change" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>04 · Morale maintenance.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="section reveal hardPart">
      <p class="eyebrow">The expensive lessons</p>
      <h2 class="sectionTitle">Some mistakes needed more than a new part.</h2>
      <p>
        I sheared bolts in the engine block. They had to be drilled out and the holes rethreaded.
        Later, excess heat bent the frame where the exhaust connects. On the ride south, the chain
        came off and I spent two hours pushing before pressing the frame back into place.
      </p>
      <figure class="frameImage">
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/bent-frame.webp" alt="The bent section of the Puch Maxi frame near the exhaust mounting point" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>The frame bent where heat from the exhaust met the leg; it was pressed back into place.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <section class="resolution reveal">
      <div class="resolutionText">
        <p class="eyebrow">The road</p>
        <h2 class="sectionTitle">Hold on long enough to ride it.</h2>
        <p>
          There was rarely a perfect tool, angle or amount of leverage. Often the only way through
          was to try every sensible method, then every plausible bodge, and accept that effort
          could not be sidestepped.
        </p>
        <p>
          It took years and I nearly gave up. The Puch may still decide not to work on a given day.
          But persistence eventually turned an eBay listing into a machine I could ride from
          Cambridge to London—and scoot around town looking rather good.
        </p>
      </div>
      <figure>
        <img src="/docs/puch-maxi/images/ready-to-go.webp" alt="The restored Puch Maxi ready for the journey to London" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
        <figcaption>Ready to leave Cambridge for London.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </section>

    <aside class="acknowledgement reveal" aria-label="Acknowledgement">
      <p class="eyebrow">Acknowledgement</p>
      <p>
        Thank you, Freddie, for helping me fix it countless times over many a cup of tea, for
        keeping it safe for me during my travels, and for giving me a love for tinkering and classic
        vehicles.
      </p>
    </aside>

    <ExploreNext currentHref="/projects/tech/puch-maxi" />
  </article>

  <style>
    .puchProject { --puch-red: #7d2f27; }
    .backLink {
      display: inline-block;
      margin-bottom: 1rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
      text-decoration: none;
    }
    .backLink:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 0.45rem;
      color: var(--puch-red);
      font-size: var(--font-size-xs);
      letter-spacing: 0.1em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }
    .heroImage, figure { margin: 0; }
    .heroImage {
      overflow: hidden;
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
      border-radius: 16px;
    }
    .heroImage img {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      height: min(72vh, 780px);
      object-fit: cover;
      object-position: center bottom;
    }
    figcaption {
      padding-top: 0.55rem;
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: var(--font-size-sm);
      line-height: 1.35;
    }
    .puchProject :global(.sectionTitle) { margin-bottom: 0.65rem; }
    .puchProject .section > p:not(.eyebrow),
    .resolutionText p:not(.eyebrow) {
      max-width: 58ch;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }
    .opening { max-width: 58ch; }
    .arrivalGrid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 0.72fr 1.28fr;
      gap: 1.25rem;
      margin: 0 0 3.5rem;
    }
    .arrivalGrid figure:nth-child(n + 3) { margin-top: 1rem; }
    .arrivalGrid img, .fuelPair img, .brakeSequence img, .frameImage img, .resolution img {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      border-radius: 12px;
      object-fit: cover;
    }
    .listing img, .arrival img { height: 31rem; }
    .fuelPair {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
      gap: 1.25rem;
      align-items: stretch;
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
    }
    .fuelPair img, .fuelPair video { height: 26rem; }
    .videoFigure video {
      display: block;
      width: 100%;
      border-radius: 12px;
      background: #111;
      object-fit: cover;
    }
    .brakeSequence {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1.5rem 1.25rem;
      margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
    }
    .brakeSequence img { aspect-ratio: 4 / 3; }
    .hardPart { max-width: none; }
    .frameImage { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
    .frameImage img { max-height: 42rem; }
    .resolution {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(18rem, 0.85fr);
      gap: 2.25rem;
      align-items: center;
      margin: 4rem 0 3.5rem;
      padding: 2.25rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 16px;
      background: var(--bg-elevated);
    }
    .resolution img { max-height: 35rem; }
    .acknowledgement {
      max-width: 58ch;
      margin: 0 0 4rem;
      padding: 1.5rem 0 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    }
    .acknowledgement p:last-child {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--text);
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.55;
    }

    @media (max-width: 720px) {
      .arrivalGrid, .fuelPair, .brakeSequence, .resolution { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
      .heroImage img { height: min(64vh, 640px); }
      .listing img, .arrival img, .fuelPair img, .fuelPair video { height: auto; max-height: 34rem; }
      .arrivalGrid figure:nth-child(n + 3) { margin-top: 0; }
      .resolution { margin: 3rem 0; padding: 1.25rem; }
      .acknowledgement { margin-bottom: 3rem; }
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
